{"availability":"available","full":"QuentinBretl/r3f-resilience","name":"r3f-resilience","description":"Two silent WebGL failures reproduced on purpose in a React Three Fiber demo - and four widely repeated fixes, three of which do not survive being measured.","category":"Design","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-02T23:19:36Z","updated":"2026-09-03T21:12:25Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://r3f-resilience.vercel.app","topics":["debugging","postprocessing","react-three-fiber","threejs","webgl","webgl-context-loss"],"demo":"https://r3f-resilience.vercel.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T13:45:20.810Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T13:45:20.810Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T13:45:20.810Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T05:41:16.381Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-08T06:38:18.201Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-10T15:03:43.402Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-15T23:48:13.742Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-19T13:45:20.810Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Three.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A React Three Fiber scene that breaks on purpose. One WebGL failure that nothing in JavaScript can see, one that floods the driver until the tab gives up, and a counter on the page that lets you watch both happen.","It comes out of Lycanthropia, a 40k-line multiplayer browser game — private, and staying that way — where this happened for real, on other people's hardware, during sessions that lasted an hour. What made these failures expensive was not that they are hard to fix. It is that nothing in JavaScript ever sees them: no exception, no error boundary, no rejected promise, no failed request. The scene stops being right, the logs stay clean, and users describe it as \"slow\".","Which is also why so much of the advice about them is wrong in a way nobody notices. If you cannot see the failure, you cannot see that your fix did nothing. Four of the fixes everyone repeats are checked here. Three do not survive."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/QuentinBretl/r3f-resilience/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"d0bb071c8a35eef40b1995dc65793c601d2d08cbc1be44d88fd26f054c729259","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T05:41:16.493Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T23:48:13.866Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A React Three Fiber scene that breaks on purpose. One WebGL failure that nothing in JavaScript can see, one that floods the driver until the tab gives up, and a counter on the page that lets you watch both happen.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/QuentinBretl/r3f-resilience/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"d0bb071c8a35eef40b1995dc65793c601d2d08cbc1be44d88fd26f054c729259","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/QuentinBretl/r3f-resilience/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T23:48:13.866Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-09-03T21:12:25Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/QuentinBretl/r3f-resilience/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T23:48:13.867Z","hash":"d0bb071c8a35eef40b1995dc65793c601d2d08cbc1be44d88fd26f054c729259","originalBytes":9972,"storedBytes":9972,"truncated":false},"lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T23:48:13.868Z","demoHealth":{"url":"https://r3f-resilience.vercel.app/","attemptedAt":"2026-10-13T20:14:20.490Z","probeVersion":3,"status":"working","checkedAt":"2026-10-13T20:14:20.490Z","lastWorkingAt":"2026-10-13T20:14:20.490Z","target":"https://r3f-resilience.vercel.app/","failureCount":0,"consecutiveTemporaryFailures":0,"nextCheckAt":"2026-10-20T20:14:20.490Z"},"previewAttemptAt":"2026-10-13T20:14:20.490Z","previewCheck":{"url":"https://r3f-resilience.vercel.app/","attemptedAt":"2026-10-13T20:14:20.490Z","consecutiveFailures":0,"status":"captured","reason":null,"nextCheckAt":"2026-10-20T20:14:20.490Z"},"screenshots":[{"src":"previews/f48046dbc96d9d744c827231.jpg","kind":"demo","capturedAt":"2